    {
      "id": 1,
      "meaning": "The outer edge or border of something. In this verse, the fringes of God's ways are just the outer edge, a small part of all He does.",
      "sources": [
        "Webster's 1913",
        "Webster's 1828"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "meaning": "A decorated edge on a piece of clothing, made of loose threads or cords. God told Israel to wear them on their cloaks to remind them of His commands.",
